{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And you shall place on the arrangement.</b> Beside each arrangement, a handbreadth of space between the two arrangements upon the pure part of the table — as in 'and upon it the bed of Menasheh.'" "<b>On the arrangement.</b> Just as 'the arrangement' mentioned there refers to two arrangements, so too 'the arrangement' mentioned here refers to two arrangements. <b>[On the arrangement</b> — together with the arrangement.]" "<b>And it shall be for bread for a memorial.</b> Rabbi Shimon says: 'memorial' is stated here and 'memorial' is stated elsewhere; just as there it is a full handful, so too here a full handful."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:54.292988444Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}